$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}])=3([\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" "answer-0f783940-c57e-5b76-b2a2-204a0ec5ec07" "answer-0dad9073-478b-54b1-a7af-14e9b549d134" "answer-9d1db3e7-b40d-5dd2-8056-ba5fbb14c5dc" "answer-a46cedc9-7f50-57d8-8219-01fc7f258e44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/id #uuid "cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}]" 