{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5\\end{aligned}])=3([\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 15\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 30 \\\\ -3 & -15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-843e0ee2-2793-547f-b5b3-9f47090c1d93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-843e0ee2-2793-547f-b5b3-9f47090c1d93" :answer-field/id #uuid "843e0ee2-2793-547f-b5b3-9f47090c1d93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-61598bc1-09c8-541d-a2bc-495d7aa9e5da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4cadc966-a1c1-5a9a-b852-d767b4eda976" "answer-46954ab0-964a-57ab-8fa8-0e59d5360640" "answer-965ed177-569f-5e7f-8162-88c02d3a166d" "answer-61598bc1-09c8-541d-a2bc-495d7aa9e5da" "answer-a0550c2c-46e7-5b33-8b4a-ff7f9477e256"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cadc966-a1c1-5a9a-b852-d767b4eda976" :answer/id #uuid "4cadc966-a1c1-5a9a-b852-d767b4eda976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46954ab0-964a-57ab-8fa8-0e59d5360640" :answer/id #uuid "46954ab0-964a-57ab-8fa8-0e59d5360640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-965ed177-569f-5e7f-8162-88c02d3a166d" :answer/id #uuid "965ed177-569f-5e7f-8162-88c02d3a166d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}36 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 44\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61598bc1-09c8-541d-a2bc-495d7aa9e5da" :answer/id #uuid "61598bc1-09c8-541d-a2bc-495d7aa9e5da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 30 \\\\ -3 & -15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0550c2c-46e7-5b33-8b4a-ff7f9477e256" :answer/id #uuid "a0550c2c-46e7-5b33-8b4a-ff7f9477e256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 30 \\\\ 3 & 15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-91187964-9e5b-5ba1-ba20-ee13e95e1abc" :question/id #uuid "91187964-9e5b-5ba1-ba20-ee13e95e1abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-269386" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}2{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=2(y{x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2([\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7\\end{aligned}])=2([\\begin{aligned}-18 & 42 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-36 & 84 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-88c7f20f-d80e-5b0b-9793-df75c33050d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-88c7f20f-d80e-5b0b-9793-df75c33050d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "88c7f20f-d80e-5b0b-9793-df75c33050d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f3e66d10-d942-55ef-95e9-74b83106f646" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b93066e-bfc5-5a06-b179-a89fa229c358" "answer-f3e66d10-d942-55ef-95e9-74b83106f646" "answer-96c28f9d-4d38-536d-af70-b7f7748daffc" "answer-05b61bf9-e784-5e7f-b97d-887c2be9e118" "answer-8e2431b9-469d-505f-9148-092565ac052a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b93066e-bfc5-5a06-b179-a89fa229c358" :answer/id #uuid "2b93066e-bfc5-5a06-b179-a89fa229c358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 42 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3e66d10-d942-55ef-95e9-74b83106f646" :answer/id #uuid "f3e66d10-d942-55ef-95e9-74b83106f646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-36 & 84 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96c28f9d-4d38-536d-af70-b7f7748daffc" :answer/id #uuid "96c28f9d-4d38-536d-af70-b7f7748daffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & -42 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05b61bf9-e784-5e7f-b97d-887c2be9e118" :answer/id #uuid "05b61bf9-e784-5e7f-b97d-887c2be9e118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}36 & -84 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2431b9-469d-505f-9148-092565ac052a" :answer/id #uuid "8e2431b9-469d-505f-9148-092565ac052a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}84 & -36 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d4b3e437-844d-5303-9430-632a3c10c221" :question/id #uuid "d4b3e437-844d-5303-9430-632a3c10c221" :question/math-academy-id "q-269468" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$36$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)={y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}({y}^{T}y)=2y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=2{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}..\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $2$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =2y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =2(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =2([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 20 \\\\ -18 & 36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de612167-821b-5b67-906f-3d3657d23ecc" "answer-field-9895d1a7-3a44-57ea-b956-04e03dd84e75"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de612167-821b-5b67-906f-3d3657d23ecc" :answer-field/id #uuid "de612167-821b-5b67-906f-3d3657d23ecc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e1ebc777-798d-542b-b2d8-06dd005a4949" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1ebc777-798d-542b-b2d8-06dd005a4949"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1ebc777-798d-542b-b2d8-06dd005a4949" :answer/id #uuid "e1ebc777-798d-542b-b2d8-06dd005a4949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9895d1a7-3a44-57ea-b956-04e03dd84e75" :answer-field/id #uuid "9895d1a7-3a44-57ea-b956-04e03dd84e75" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-64dc66b1-5c3d-5c72-b336-2800c7a43bf5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64dc66b1-5c3d-5c72-b336-2800c7a43bf5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64dc66b1-5c3d-5c72-b336-2800c7a43bf5" :answer/id #uuid "64dc66b1-5c3d-5c72-b336-2800c7a43bf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-77050388-523c-51b2-a4cd-6bc076f8c7c6" :question/id #uuid "77050388-523c-51b2-a4cd-6bc076f8c7c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-269479" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"8px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"45px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"45px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"8px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{3}.$ Then, $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y)=y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}={y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -70 \\\\ 0 & -35 \\\\ 0 & 63\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c5eddbec-fc63-5a81-8892-f999adcf5ee9" "answer-field-4961b210-cf39-5c5d-9780-93686b4c259c" "answer-field-8ec0e1fd-84d9-5db8-b8ef-dcebc1ff50ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c5eddbec-fc63-5a81-8892-f999adcf5ee9" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5eddbec-fc63-5a81-8892-f999adcf5ee9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-48db2235-143d-5295-b583-2370275dc856" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48db2235-143d-5295-b583-2370275dc856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48db2235-143d-5295-b583-2370275dc856" :answer/id #uuid "48db2235-143d-5295-b583-2370275dc856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4961b2