5662c2c-d0a2-5e1c-b319-cae7bd255ca0"] ["question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/id #uuid "55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226"] ["question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/math-academy-id "q-269371"] ["question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}])=3([\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d"] ["answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/id #uuid "cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787"] ["answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 