" :answer-field/choices "answer-9d1db3e7-b40d-5dd2-8056-ba5fbb14c5dc"] ["answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/choices "answer-a46cedc9-7f50-57d8-8219-01fc7f258e44"] ["question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d"] [17592186204080 :knowledge-point/questions "question-55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226"] ["question-46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec" :question/id #uuid "46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec"] ["question-46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-269374"] ["question-46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)={y}^{T}Ax$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-8b6efc19-f8ac-54c7-9b1b-33f93190cd99" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6efc19-f8ac-54c7-9b1b-33f93190cd99"] ["answer-49b3a6e4-a83e-5aa7-80cd-5b9