j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{3}.$ Then, $L(A)={y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}({y}^{T}y)=2y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=2{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $2$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =2y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =2(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =2([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -32 & -32 \\\\ 16 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-def3b7cd-4317-5941-a403-30fe46331281" :question/difficulty :question.d